                        {
                            Name: "Fair winds",
                            Actions: [
                                {
                                    Type: "CLOSE_DIALOG"
                                }
                            ],
                            Label: "leave_button"
                        }
                    ],
                    Texts: [
                        {
                            Text: "(A weathered deckhand leans on a bollard, watching the west quay like the tide owes him money.) Mind the edge. Stone's slick where the harbour spits over it. Lost a good pair of boots to that gap and I was still wearing them."
                        },
                        {
                            Text: "Half the crews out of this port sail short a hand these days. Wages come up light, so the able-bodied sign on somewhere the coin still weighs what it says. Me, I know this quay too well to leave it. Every plank has a grudge and I know all their names."
                        }
                    ],
                    Name: "Deckhand Rocco",
                    Label: "default"
                }
            ]
